      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "In low-cost-of-living, rural areas, a mandated increase in the minimum wage can be a significant operational strain for small, tight-margin businesses like a local cafe. While the absolute cost increase might be less than in a high-cost city, it can feel more impactful because the overall operational budget is already lean. These changes often force small owners to absorb the higher labor cost, potentially leading to price increases for the consumer or a review of the total staff size and efficiency.",
